==English==
{{was wotd|2015|December|26}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|gulpen}}, probably from {{der|en|vls|-}} or {{der|en|dum|gulpen}}, {{m|dum|golpen}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. Perhaps of {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitative}} origin, or related to {{cog|nl|galpen|t=to roar, squeal}}, {{cog|en|galp}}, {{m|en|gaup|t=to gape}}.

Related to {{cog|nds-de|gulpen|t=to gush out, belch, gulp}}, {{cog|fy|gjalpe}}, {{m|fy|gjalpje}}, {{m|fy|gjealpje|t=to gush, spurt forth}}, {{cog|da|gulpe}}, {{m|da|gylpe|t=to gulp up, disgorge}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|glapa|t=to gulp down}}, {{cog|ang|galpettan|t=to gulp down, eat greedily, devour}}. More at {{l|en|galp}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡʌlp/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-gulp.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌlp|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[usual]] [[amount#Noun|amount]] [[swallow#Verb|swallowed]].
#: {{synonyms|en|slug}}
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|year=1934|passage=What the liquor was I do not know, but it was not so strong but that I could swallow it in great '''gulps''' and found it less burning than my burning throat.}}
# The sound of swallowing, sometimes indicating fear.
#* {{RQ:Sinclair Jungle|chapter=17|passage=Little Stanislovas was also trembling, and all but too frightened to speak. "They — they sent me to tell you — " he said, with a '''gulp'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=James Charles Collins; Jerry I. Porras|title=Built to Last: Successful Habits of Visionary Companies
|passage=Indeed, the envisioned future should produce a bit of "the '''gulp''' factor" {{...}}, there should be an almost audible "'''gulp'''".}}
# {{lb|en|rare|computing}} An unspecified small number of [[byte]]s, often two.

