===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To swallow eagerly, or in large draughts; to swallow up; to take down in one swallow.
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:drink}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1782|author=w:William Cowper|title=Table-Talk|passage=He does not swallow, but he '''gulps''' it down.}}
# To [[react]] [[nervous]]ly by swallowing.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1930|author=w:P. G. Wodehouse|title=A Damsel in Distress|page=198|year_published=2004
|passage=The man eyed Percy with a chilly eye. "Well," he said, "What's troublin you?" Percy '''gulped'''. The man's mere appearance was a sedative. "Er-nothing! […]"}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Carl Deuker|title=High Heat|page=140
|passage=I'd always been nervous-excited; this was nervous-terrified. When I finished puking, I sat down '''gulping''' air for a while, trying to pull myself together.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Nancy Anne Nicholson|title=Thin White Female in No Acute Distress: A Memoir|page=187
|passage=My heart was beating madly and I was '''gulping''' nervous energy.}}

